# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Derived packages: declare what you own below this line
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# This repository is the template, and the template owns everything: there are
# deliberately no `merge=keepours` entries here. Ownership is declared only in a
# derived package, by appending lines to the BOTTOM of its own copy of this
# file, underneath the template's lines above. Template-owned is the default and
# there is no positive list, so anything a derived package does not claim here
# keeps arriving from `git pull template main`.
#
# The merge driver named by those lines resolves to the derived package's side
# unconditionally, so template changes to those paths are dropped rather than
# conflicting. For this template the expected derived-owned surface is:
#
#     sdk.json               merge=keepours
#     README.md              merge=keepours
#     src/ApiRoute.php       merge=keepours
#     src/Models/**          merge=keepours
#     factories/**           merge=keepours
#     .env                   merge=keepours
#
# `src/ApiRoute.php`, `src/Models/**` and `factories/**` are generated from the
# package's own OpenAPI document. They are regenerated, never merged.
#
# Two categories must never appear as `merge=keepours`:
#
#   * Lockfiles. Resolving one to this side pins the package below what the
#     newly merged code requires, and the failure surfaces later as a missing
#     symbol rather than as a conflict. Let them conflict and regenerate.
#   * Anything that differs only for branding. Move that difference into
#     sdk.json instead, so the file itself can keep merging cleanly.
#
# The driver is not carried by this file. Each fresh clone must run, once:
#
#     git config merge.keepours.driver true
#
# Without it git falls back to an ordinary conflicting merge and says nothing,
# so a clone that skipped the command looks fine until the first merge resolves
# the wrong way. `./run check-template` fails when it is unset.
